                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79952215-c46d-391e-aa2a-d1cc8da15a2f",
                        "entry_id": "2607d719-cdd4-3bd5-af80-1e6e22f2c614",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Finger-like."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47c62474-7c79-48b3-a2bb-d38abf6a512a",
                                "sense_id": "79952215-c46d-391e-aa2a-d1cc8da15a2f",
                                "text": "The larger ossicles are striated on the surface, the striae being produced along the anterior margin so as to give it a dactylous appearance; the median striation is longest, and extends to the point of the rhomboidally-shaped scale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0880e69-187f-44a7-a582-e9255c6a84fe",
                                "sense_id": "79952215-c46d-391e-aa2a-d1cc8da15a2f",
                                "text": "basal dactylous cell of the sterile branchlets tapering into the conical and strongly acuminate ultimate cell ; basal dactylous cell of the fertile branchlets rounded at the apex;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f943940e-911b-4940-a533-a6974bb38615",
                                "sense_id": "79952215-c46d-391e-aa2a-d1cc8da15a2f",
                                "text": "The unfortunate fact that there are no dactylous pedicellariae to be found in the specimen under consideration prevents reaching a definite conclusion. The dactylous pedicellariae of A. owstoni and A. coriaceum are very different— 3-valved and of a very primitive type in the former, 5-valved and of a highly finished type in the latter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8c1b086-9812-4855-bcbe-6906e292a137",
                                "sense_id": "79952215-c46d-391e-aa2a-d1cc8da15a2f",
                                "text": "The dactylous type reaches its extreme development in species of Araeosoma, where it consists of four or five jaws drawn out into a long narrow shape, topped by a terminal disciform expansion."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dac6e5b8-dbec-3425-ba72-388bb38fadf7",
                        "entry_id": "2607d719-cdd4-3bd5-af80-1e6e22f2c614",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having or pertaining to fingers or toes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "add1b520-1abc-4928-bde7-41796b560dde",
                                "sense_id": "dac6e5b8-dbec-3425-ba72-388bb38fadf7",
                                "text": "Congenital dactylous malformations in 15 of 401 malformed lambs ( 3.7 percent ) are described ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20102ae4-3f09-42fe-b35e-8f1621b8d6e3",
                                "sense_id": "dac6e5b8-dbec-3425-ba72-388bb38fadf7",
                                "text": "Although the Famennian tetrapods have dactylous limbs and more heavily constructed vertebral columns than lobe-finned fishes, they still appear to have been largely aquatic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88930849-7745-4c05-96b4-aa118cd01dc7",
                                "sense_id": "dac6e5b8-dbec-3425-ba72-388bb38fadf7",
                                "text": "We presume that they made at least brief ventures onto land because of their dactylous limbs and modified limb girdles."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "83b207f5-ef22-33cb-a7d2-46950f0e0854",
                        "entry_id": "2607d719-cdd4-3bd5-af80-1e6e22f2c614",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to dactyls."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14f53879-e3c4-4f02-bff6-2df6ad3117ed",
                                "sense_id": "83b207f5-ef22-33cb-a7d2-46950f0e0854",
                                "text": "There is a charming sonnet at the end, whcih comes to our lips like a draught of vintage that hath been Cooled a long age in the deep deved earth; and is might refreshing after the dactylous jolting of two hundred pages, and indicates the possession of original powers in the writer."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
